:\n18:    - **Signed URL Expiration during export generation** ([`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) / [`record-eb2ad86fcb`](file:///works\n<truncated 9833 bytes>\ns).\n102:    - Add automated failure injection to test checkpoint resumption and verify 100% parity against source database rows.\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: ## 5. Important Uncertainty\n107: \n108: 1. **Submission Date of Ticket [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json):**\n109:    - The ticket was imported on `2026-09-07T18:00:00Z`, but its `submitted_at` timestamp is `null` (unknown). Although the matching operational incident ([`record-eb2ad86fcb`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json)) occurred on `2026-08-31T15:00:00Z`, the exact time the customer submitted their ticket cannot be established from this snapshot and must not be invented.\n110: 2. **Format Scope of Cursor Resumption Defect:**\n111:    - The missing-row warning was recorded for NDJSON in [`record-6a8741fe3b`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json). It is currently uncertain whether the cursor checkpoint dropping rows is isolated to the NDJSON serializer or exists in the shared database cursor pagination layer across all formats.\n112: 3. **EU Workspaces Reliability and Compliance:**\n113:    - Per [`record-d46f9580f1`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md), EU workspaces were explicitly excluded from the 2026-09-07 missing-row audit. Their large-scale export failure rate and cursor stability remain unverified in the current evidence.\n114: 4. **Behavior at Higher Scales (>2.1M rows):**\n115:    - The observed failures occurred at 1.8M and 2.1M rows. Workspaces exceeding these volumes may encounter additional unobserved resource limits (e.g. disk spool exhaustion or global worker timeouts).\n116: 5. **Snapshot Boundary:**\n117:    - This analysis is strictly confined to the local snapshot as of `2026-09-08`/`2026-09-09`. Live production telemetry, external database connections, and customer communications are not accessible in this environment.\n118: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":103,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:12:50Z","content":"The dated recommendation for the export feedback follow-through has been documented in [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Findings & Decision\n\n* **Do Not Close the Support Tickets:** Tickets [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) (submitted date unknown, imported 2026-09-07T18:00:00Z) and [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) (submitted 2026-09-06T14:31:00Z) do not predate the rollout. The `\"age_days\": 14` field in [`record-b851997b7c.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) represents days elapsed since the August 25 rollout of [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md), not ticket age.\n* **Corroborated Root Causes on Large Workspaces (>1M rows):**\n  1. **Premature Signed URL Expiry (\"takes too long / link expired\"):** Corroborated by [`record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json) (1.8M CSV rows). The background worker successfully wrote all 1,800,000 rows in 1,184 seconds (~19.7 min), but because signed URLs are generated at job start with a 900-second (15-minute) TTL, download attempts fail with HTTP 403.\n  2. **Silent Record Drop on Checkpoint Resumption (\"missing rows\"):** Corroborated by [`record-6a8741fe3b.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json) (2.1M NDJSON rows). The export finished with HTTP 200 but dropped 60,559 records due to a cursor offset omission flagged by `\"account relation scan resumed after cursor checkpoint\"`.\n  3. **Why Earlier Audits Missed This:** The rollout smoke check ([`record-7c21733985.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md)) only validated 50,000 rows, and the 100% parity dashboard audit ([`record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md)) explicitly excluded NDJSON, large workspaces, EU workspaces, and URL-expiry failures.\n* **Next Useful Actions:** Prepare reversible changes within the product to defer signed URL minting until worker completion (or generate fresh URLs on demand) and correct the account relation scan cursor checkpoint resume logic, accompanied by new 1M+ and 2M+ row verification fixtures.\n\nPlease review [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md) for the complete analysis, citation of source paths and IDs, and documented uncertainties.","thinking":"**Reviewing export feedback instructions**\n\nReviewing the initial instructions confirms the focus: address support reports of incomplete or slow ledger exports. The objective is to evaluate previous actions and determine the best path forward.\nThe specified workspace and starting files are confirmed.\nThe attached source archive requires reading.\n\n\n"}
